{"name":"Enterprise","hex":"#65788c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Enterprise","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States:\nA city in Coffee County, Alabama.\nAn unincorporated community in Amador County, California.\nAn unincorporated community in Lake County, California.\nAn unincorporated community in Volusia County, Florida.\nAn unincorporated community in Spencer County, Indiana.\nA minor city in Dickinson County, Kansas.\nA town in Clarke County, Mississippi.\nAn unincorporated community in Union County, Mississippi.\nAn unincorporated community in Linn County, Missouri.\nAn unincorporated community in Shelby County, Missouri.\nAn unincorporated town and census-designated place in Clark County, Nevada.\nAn unincorporated community in Hocking County, Ohio.\nAn unincorporated community in Preble County, Ohio.\nA city, the county seat of Wallowa County, Oregon.\nA city in Washington County, Utah.\nA census-designated place in Morgan County, Utah.\nAn unincorporated community in Wirt County, West Virginia.\nA town and unincorporated community in Oneida County, Wisconsin.","A city in Coffee County, Alabama."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Enterprise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Enterprise GP Holdings","blocks":[{"text":"Enterprise GP Holdings was a midstream energy holding company based in Houston, Texas, that made its debut on the Fortune 500 list at #177 in 2007. It had its corporate headquarters in the Enterprise Plaza in Downtown Houston."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/EnterprisePlazaHoustonTX.JPG/330px-EnterprisePlazaHoustonTX.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enterprise_GP_Holdings","wikidata":"Q5380315"},{"title":"Enterprise plc","blocks":[{"text":"Enterprise plc was a support services company originally based in Farington in Lancashire, England. Its core markets were local authorities and utility sectors. It has recently been integrated into Ferrovial's UK company, Amey plc."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1f/Enterprise_logo.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enterprise_plc","wikidata":"Q5380400"},{"title":"Enterprise (NX-01)","blocks":[{"text":"Enterprise (NX-01) is the fictional spaceship that serves as the primary setting of the American science fiction television series Star Trek: Enterprise. The ship predates the other Starfleet ships named Enterprise and was first seen in the pilot episode \"Broken Bow\". Its missions included an initial period of deep space exploration and a mission into the Delphic Expanse following the Xindi attack on Earth; it was also instrumental in the formation of the United Federation of Planets with the Vulcans, Andorians and Tellarites."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/74/Enterprise_NX-01.jpg/330px-Enterprise_NX-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enterprise_(NX-01)","wikidata":"Q20074"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Enterprise_Liverpool.jpg/500px-Enterprise_Liverpool.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Enterprise_Liverpool.jpg/1280px-Enterprise_Liverpool.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Enterprise_Liverpool.jpg/500px-Enterprise_Liverpool.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Enterprise Liverpool van on Hanover Street","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEnterprise_Liverpool.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/2002-2005_Ford_Thunderbi